<http://data.silknow.org/object/bd45839b-64da-371f-95f8-6a20e4b187af/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Man’s waistcoat with a round neckline, curving fronts and skirts reaching to the top of the thigh.  Each front has a pocket and pointed pocket flap.  The fronts and pocket flaps are made of white silk satin, the back of white silk twill.  The waistcoat and pockets are lined with fustian, pocket flaps with white silk satin; the skirt linings and front facings are white silk twill. The waistcoat is quilted with vertical lines of tambouring in silver-gilt filé and green silk thread.  It is embroidered-to-shape with tambouring in silver-gilt filé and silk thread in shades of green and pink, and couched silver-gilt spangles, in a pattern of abstract floral sprigs, on the pocket flaps, front edges and hems and around the front neck. There are 12 worked buttonholes along the left front, with 12 embroidered buttons on the right front.\n\nThe waistcoat was altered for size in the 18th century; a triangle of glazed linen was stitched into the centre-back seam."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/bd45839b-64da-371f-95f8-6a20e4b187af> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/bd45839b-64da-371f-95f8-6a20e4b187af>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Man’s waistcoat with a round neckline, curving fronts and skirts reaching to the top of the thigh.  Each front has a pocket and pointed pocket flap.  The fronts and pocket flaps are made of white silk satin, the back of white silk twill.  The waistcoat and pockets are lined with fustian, pocket flaps with white silk satin; the skirt linings and front facings are white silk twill. The waistcoat is quilted with vertical lines of tambouring in silver-gilt filé and green silk thread.  It is embroidered-to-shape with tambouring in silver-gilt filé and silk thread in shades of green and pink, and couched silver-gilt spangles, in a pattern of abstract floral sprigs, on the pocket flaps, front edges and hems and around the front neck. There are 12 worked buttonholes along the left front, with 12 embroidered buttons on the right front.\n\nThe waistcoat was altered for size in the 18th century; a triangle of glazed linen was stitched into the centre-back seam."@en , "Man's waistcoat, 1775-80, British; white silk satin, quilted, tamboured with silk and silver thread, spangles"@en ;
